+# NAP SDL_GPU CMP part transform A/B (2026-10-19)
+
+This diagnostic selects the `br_tail_lod1` component from the Bretonia Elite
+CMP, assembles the real CMP construct hierarchy, applies that component's
+transform to its VMesh positions, normals and tangents, then draws the selected
+indexed material through the production Freelancer PBR shader on SDL_GPU/Vulkan.
+It tests one component and one material draw; it does not render a complete
+ship or the game's render graph.
+
+## Input provenance
+
+The seven archive inputs listed in [`provenance.json`](provenance.json) were
+staged from files under `Data/NAP/`. The active manifest is
+[`active.json`](active.json). Immediately before both runs, `nexus-pack verify`
+reported all seven entries valid. The archive size was 111,401,506 bytes and
+its SHA-256 was
+`8031335a3380a197fe6d53c073aff57a107473544afac81c25e9b55d752e84c2`.
+The runtime application root was
+`Data/NAP/.runtime-test-stage/br-elite-renderer-20261019/application`; it had
+the active package directory and no loose `DATA` directory.
+
+## Result
+
+Both runs selected the same component, indexed mesh, material and 282 indices:
+
+- CMP object: `br_tail_lod1`; assembled local transform position
+  `(0.000, -0.543, 7.960)`.
+- VMesh: `099A3548`; material CRC `F01764A2`, `br_elite_lod`, diffuse
+  `br_elite_256.tga`; base vertex 646.
+- Surface off and on both passed all four readback coverage probes.
+- Surface on resolved `nm_ships_br_elite_256` from
+  `normalmaps_ships_auto_1.txm` and uploaded the BC5 normal plus BC4 roughness
+  and metallic maps.
+- Comparing the complete diagnostic captures gives normalized RGB RMSE
+  `0.123275`; the captures also include synthetic smoke and shadow panels.
+
+| Surface maps off | Surface maps on |
+|---|---|
+| ![Tail part with Surface maps off](surface-off.png) | ![Tail part with Surface maps on](surface-on.png) |
+
+The side-by-side capture is [`comparison.png`](comparison.png). Full SDL logs
+are in [`surface-off.log`](surface-off.log) and [`surface-on.log`](surface-on.log).
+
+The Release `lancer` build succeeded with zero warnings and zero errors before
+these runs. Both processes exited 0 using Mesa/Vulkan on Intel Haswell; Mesa
+reported incomplete Haswell Vulkan support. This proves the selected non-root
+part transform and one mapped material reach the SDL_GPU production PBR draw.
+It does not validate all CMP components, full-ship composition, material parity,
+lighting quality, performance, or another GPU/backend.
